Interoperability: SignalDeck talks to the radio module built into supported phones. It contains none of the phone
maker's software. At run time it uses the phone's own system libraries and services (for example the serial-port
library and the audio service already installed on the phone); tiny-stubs/ only declares the names of those system
interfaces so the app can be compiled. Those components remain the property of their owners.


